        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.9,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": "MATHEMATICS"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.248,
            0.146,
            0.748,
            0.192
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{\\mathrm{AB}}{\\mathrm{RQ}}=\\frac{3.8}{7.6}=\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{\\mathrm{BC}}{\\mathrm{QP}}=\\frac{6}{12}=\\frac{1}{2} \\text { and } \\frac{\\mathrm{CA}}{\\mathrm{PR}}=\\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{6 \\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{1}{2}",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.224,
            0.176,
            0.243
          ],
          "content": "That is,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.241,
            0.209,
            0.412,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{\\mathrm{AB}}{\\mathrm{RQ}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{BC}}{\\mathrm{QP}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{CA}}{\\mathrm{PR}}",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.269,
            0.135,
            0.287
          ],
          "content": "So,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.277,
            0.268,
            0.455,
            0.288
          ],
          "content": "\\Delta   \\mathrm { A B C } \\sim \\Delta   \\mathrm { R Q P }",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.746,
            0.268,
            0.9,
            0.289
          ],
          "content": "(SSS similarity)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.301,
            0.205,
            0.321
          ],
          "content": "Therefore,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.301,
            0.426,
            0.32
          ],
          "content": "\\angle C = \\angle  P",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.492,
            0.301,
            0.901,
            0.323
          ],
          "content": "(Corresponding angles of similar triangles)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.328,
            0.142,
            0.346
          ],
          "content": "But"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.327,
            0.559,
            0.347
          ],
          "content": "\\angle C = 180^{\\circ} - \\angle A - \\angle B",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.687,
            0.327,
            0.9,
            0.349
          ],
          "content": "(Angle sum property)"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.351,
            0.358,
            0.604,
            0.379
          ],
          "content": "=   180^{\\circ} - 80^{\\circ} - 60^{\\circ} = 40^{\\circ}",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.386,
            0.135,
            0.403
          ],
          "content": "So,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.31,
            0.384,
            0.418,
            0.403
          ],
          "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { P } = 4 0 ^ { \\circ }",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.41,
            0.352,
            0.429
          ],
          "content": "**Example 6 :** In Fig. 6.31,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.216,
            0.435,
            0.435,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": "OA. OB = OC. OD.",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.459,
            0.495,
            0.479
          ],
          "content": "Show that $\\angle \\mathrm{A} = \\angle \\mathrm{C}   and   \\angle \\mathrm{B} = \\angle \\mathrm{D}.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.485,
            0.562,
            0.505
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** $OA. OB = OC. OD$ (Given)"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.601,
            0.383,
            0.875,
            0.544
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_19_image_21.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.532,
            0.135,
            0.549
          ],
          "content": "So,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.274,
            0.518,
            0.562,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{OA}{OC} = \\frac{OD}{OB}\\tag{1}",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_23.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.568,
            0.244,
            0.587
          ],
          "content": "Also, we have"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.385,
            0.567,
            0.899,
            0.588
          ],
          "content": "$\\angle AOD = \\angle COB$ (Vertically opposite angles) (2)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.593,
            0.84,
            0.613
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, from (1) and (2), $\\Delta  AOD  \\sim \\Delta  COB$ (SAS similarity criterion)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.619,
            0.135,
            0.637
          ],
          "content": "So,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.376,
            0.618,
            0.9,
            0.658
          ],
          "content": "$\\angle A = \\angle C$ and $\\angle \\mathrm{D} = \\angle \\mathrm{B}$ (Corresponding angles of similar triangles)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.671,
            0.503,
            0.777
          ],
          "content": "**Example 7 :** A girl of height 90 cm is walking away from the base of a lamp-post at a speed of 1.2 m/s. If the lamp is 3.6 m above the ground, find the length of her shadow after 4 seconds."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
            0.966,
            0.564,
            0.983
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.783,
            0.502,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** Let AB denote the lamp-post and CD the girl after walking for 4 seconds away from the lamp-post (see Fig. 6.32)."
